# Global Conventions

This is a Node.js/Express investment questionnaire app. Frontend is vanilla
JS/HTML/CSS in `public/`, backend logic lives in `server.js`. UI copy and
business-domain text are in Russian; code, identifiers, comments, commit
messages and rule files are in English.

## Stack & Layout

- Backend: `server.js` (Express, single `POST /calculate` endpoint).
- Frontend: `public/index.html`, `public/script.js`, `public/style.css`.
- Entry: `npm start` -> `node server.js` on `PORT` (default `5000`).
- Do not introduce build tooling, bundlers, or TypeScript without explicit
  request — keep the project zero-build.

## Editing Rules

- Preserve the existing data contract between frontend and `/calculate`
  (sections `A`, `B`, `C1`, `C2`, `D`, `E`, `F`, `G`). Any change to request
  or response shape must be reflected in BOTH `server.js` and `public/script.js`
  in the same edit.
- Russian month names and seasonality keys (`winter`/`spring`/`summer`/
  `autumn`) are part of the contract — do not translate them.
- Monetary values are stored in roubles and returned in thousands (divided by
  1000). Keep this convention; never mix units silently.
- Financial formulas (IRR bisection, NPV, PI, payback) live in `server.js`.
  When changing them, document the reasoning in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Any new UI feature in `public/` must pass the visual validation workflow in
  `.cursor/rules/visual-validation.mdc` using
  `.cursor/context/visual-regulator.md` as baseline.

## Code Style (English only inside code)

- Variable names, function names, file names: English, `camelCase` for JS.
- Code comments: English, only when explaining non-obvious intent.
- User-facing strings (HTML, alerts, chart labels): Russian, matching existing
  tone.

## Safety

- Never commit secrets, `.env` files, or `zipFile.zip` contents.
- Do not run destructive git commands without explicit user approval.
- Do not change `package.json` `name`, `main`, or `start` script unless asked.
